# Release secrets for scripts/release.sh and scripts/ios-appstore.sh.
#
# Copy to scripts/.env and fill in. THAT FILE IS GITIGNORED (as of 2026-07-31 - it was not
# before, which is worth knowing if you have an old checkout lying around). This example file
# is committed; never put a real value in it.
#
# app.conf holds everything that is NOT secret and is committed. If a value is safe to publish,
# it belongs there instead.

# ── iOS: App Store Connect ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# THE PREFERRED ROUTE, and the one the Mac is already set up for. `asc` is installed there
# (1.1.1 via brew) and the private key is already in place at
# ~/.appstoreconnect/private_keys/AuthKey_28U2P9D99H.p8, so the KEY ID below is the one that
# key file is named after. Only the other two need fetching.

# The API key id - the string in the AuthKey_<KEY_ID>.p8 filename.
ASC_KEY_ID=28U2P9D99H

# A UUID, and the one thing you have to go and look up. App Store Connect ->
# Users and Access -> Integrations -> App Store Connect API. It is per-TEAM, not per-app, so
# once you have it, it is the same value for every PeerLoom app.
ASC_ISSUER_ID=

# The app's NUMERIC id, which is per-app. App Store Connect -> your app -> App Information ->
# General Information -> Apple ID. It is also the number in the URL of that page.
ASC_APP_ID=

# Only if the .p8 is somewhere other than ~/.appstoreconnect/AuthKey_<ASC_KEY_ID>.p8.
#ASC_PRIVATE_KEY_PATH=

# ── iOS: the legacy fallback ────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Used only when the three above are not all set. altool with an app-specific password from
# appleid.apple.com -> Sign-In and Security -> App-Specific Passwords. Works, but it is the
# older path and Apple has been narrowing it - prefer the API key.
#ASC_APPLE_ID=
#ASC_APP_PASSWORD=

# ── Android: Play Console ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The upload keystore password and the service-account JSON path, if/when the Play upload is
# scripted. Left commented because nothing reads them yet.
#ANDROID_KEYSTORE_PASSWORD=
#ANDROID_KEY_PASSWORD=
#GOOGLE_PLAY_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=
